----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[K: g1-h1, P: g2-f3]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Let me analyze this chess position carefully.\n\n**Current Position Analysis:**\n- I'm playing as White and appear to be in a very constrained position\n- My king is on g1, and I only have 2 valid moves available\n- Black has most of their pieces still on the back rank\n- I have a bishop on c4 and some development, but my position looks critical\n\n**Evaluating the two available moves:**\n\n1. **K: g1-h1** (King moves to h1)\n   - This is a passive defensive move\n   - Moves the king into the corner, potentially worse positioning\n   - Doesn't improve my position or create threats\n   - Likely a move to escape check or avoid immediate mate threat\n\n2. **P: g2-f3** (Pawn captures on f3)\n   - This appears to be a capturing move (pawn moving diagonally)\n   - Likely capturing a Black piece on f3 (probably the knight from f3 based on board)\n   - Opens up the king position but removes an attacking piece\n   - More active than the king move\n\n**Evaluation:**\nGiven that I only have two legal moves, I'm likely in check or facing an immediate threat. The pawn capture on f3 would eliminate a checking piece (most likely a Black knight), while moving the king to h1 would just evade. Capturing is generally superior to passive retreat when possible, as it removes the opponent's attacking piece and may give me more options next turn.\n\n**Reason:**\nThe pawn capture P: g2-f3 removes Black's attacking piece (likely a knight giving check), which is better than passively moving my king into the corner. Eliminating threats by capturing is strategically sound, and this gives me a better chance to survive and potentially counterattack.\n\n**Answer:** P: g2-f3"}
