ates my most powerful remaining piece (the rook) to a central file, provides potential support for my king's escape to safety, and maintains flexibility. The rook on e1 can help control important central squares and potentially challenge Black's pieces. This move prepares better king safety while keeping tactical options open.\n\nAnswer: R: d1-e1"}
